  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "DIE+z8cWYc8IKCWe1Hgl8Vlv3us=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:48.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "## The gotcha\n\nA user with `WRITE` on a document **cannot rename it**. Renaming is not part of the document's own write permission \u2014 the name lives on the drive's node entry, so renaming is an `UPDATE_NODE` operation on the **drive** document. Grant it there, not on the document.\n\nThis catches people because \"rename\" feels like the mildest possible edit. Structurally it is not an edit to the document at all.\n\n## Drive operation types\n\nFor document drives specifically, these operation permissions are available:\n\n| Operation | What it allows |\n| --- | --- |\n| `ADD_FILE` | Create new files within the drive |\n| `ADD_FOLDER` | Create new folders within the drive |\n| `DELETE_NODE` | Delete files or folders within the drive |\n| `UPDATE_FILE` | Modify existing files within the drive |\n| `UPDATE_NODE` | Update properties of files or folders \u2014 **including renaming documents** |\n| `COPY_NODE` | Copy files or folders within the drive |\n| `MOVE_NODE` | Move files or folders within the drive |\n\n## Two orthogonal axes\n\nOperation permissions give fine-grained control over specific actions, **separate from** the general document permission levels (`READ`, `WRITE`, `ADMIN`). They are two axes, not a hierarchy: a grant on one says nothing about the other.\n\nOperation permissions are queried and granted per `(documentId, operationType)` pair, with both user and group grants:\n\n```graphql\nquery GetOperationPermissions($documentId: String!, $operationType: String!) {\n  operationPermissions(documentId: $documentId, operationType: $operationType) {\n    documentId\n    operationType\n    userPermissions { userAddress grantedBy createdAt }\n    groupPermissions { groupId group { id name } grantedBy createdAt }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe list above is drive-specific. If you need operation permissions for documents of other models, look up the available operations of the installed document-model package \u2014 the operation type is just the action name, so the vocabulary is per model.\n\n_Source: apps/academy/docs/academy/03-Build/03-BuildingUserExperiences/07-Authorization/02-DocumentPermissions.md (Powerhouse v6.2.2-dev.45)._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T12:35:48.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T12:35:48.000Z"
    }
  },
